    "effective_rank_max": 1,
    "three_axes_are_one_dimension": true,
    "frontier_invariant_to_any_single_axis_drop": true,
    "one_axis_statement": "The three declared axes span a single dimension at every support, over both the pool the frontier decides between (the seven Earth candidates) and the wider cross-body pool. Mean slope and mean 3x3 relief are mathematically the same measurement up to a direction factor bounded by 41% -- verified against the engine's own functions to floating point -- and the elevation standard deviation tracks them empirically. A Pareto frontier over these three is therefore a one-dimensional ordering and must not be reported as three lines of evidence.",
    "what_this_does_not_mean": "It does not make the lunar result wrong. It makes it smaller and more robust: a one-dimensional ordering is far more stable than a genuine three-dimensional frontier, which is consistent with the 6/6 ensemble and the 18/18 panel agreement."
  }
